      "description": "Resize the environmental advocates group to 30 participants and each other group to 5 participants by repeating its predefined judgment template. Counts are final group sizes, including the original participants.",
      "purpose": "Test whether replication of identical within-group preferences leaves numerical results unchanged when group voting powers remain equal.",
      "hypothesis": "All group weights, session weights, TOPSIS scores, and winner sets match the control despite the unequal final participant counts. This expectation applies to template replication and does not imply invariance under changes in preference composition.",
